{
  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_consensus_margin",
  "intuition": "All parents share a stable core: a pairwise preference objective using -logsigmoid of the log-prob gap (log_prob_w - log_prob_l), with clamping to keep gradients numerically stable and optional per-example weights. Some parents add a detached cost gap as a small bias term. A robust consensus is to keep the standard clamped pairwise logsigmoid, and (optionally) incorporate a detached cost gap as a bounded, weak margin shift so it cannot destabilize training when costs are noisy or missing. Using a moderate default scale between observed parent scales should preserve effective gradient magnitudes while remaining safe.",
  "pseudocode": "d = (lpw - lpl)\nmargin = -cost_coef * clamp(detach(cost_b - cost_a), -gap_clip, gap_clip)  # optional\nx = clamp(alpha * scale * d + margin, -x_clip, x_clip)\nloss = -logsigmoid(x)\nreturn mean(loss * weight_if_present)",
  "hyperparams": {
    "scale": 1.0,
    "cost_coef": 0.05,
    "gap_clip": 10.0,
    "x_clip": 20.0
  },
  "operators_used": [
    "logsigmoid",
    "clamp"
  ],
  "code": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n\n    hp = extra.get('hyperparams', {}) if isinstance(extra, dict) else {}\n    alpha = float(extra.get('alpha', hp.get('alpha', 1.0))) if isinstance(extra, dict) else 1.0\n    scale = float(hp.get('scale', 1.0))\n    cost_coef = float(hp.get('cost_coef', 0.05))\n    gap_clip = float(hp.get('gap_clip', 10.0))\n    x_clip = float(hp.get('x_clip', 20.0))\n\n    x = alpha * scale * (lpw - lpl)\n\n    # Optional detached cost-based margin shift; safe if cost fields are absent.\n    if ('cost_a' in batch) and ('cost_b' in batch) and (cost_coef != 0.0):\n        gap = (batch['cost_b'] - batch['cost_a']).detach()\n        gap = ops.clamp(gap, -gap_clip, gap_clip)\n        x = x - cost_coef * gap\n\n    x = ops.clamp(x, -x_clip, x_clip)\n    loss = -ops.logsigmoid(x)\n    if weight is not None:\n        loss = loss * weight\n    return loss.mean()",
  "theoretical_basis": "Pairwise logistic (Bradley-Terry / DPO-style) objective on the log-probability difference encourages the model to assign higher likelihood to the preferred sample. Clamping improves numerical stability. An optional detached cost-gap term acts as a bounded margin adjustment without backpropagating through the cost signal, reducing sensitivity to noisy cost estimates.",
  "implementation_hint": {
    "expects": {
      "batch": [
        "log_prob_w",
        "log_prob_l"
      ],
      "batch_optional": [
        "weight",
        "cost_a",
        "cost_b"
      ],
      "extra": [
        "alpha",
        "hyperparams"
      ],
      "extra_hyperparams_optional": [
        "scale",
        "cost_coef",
        "gap_clip",
        "x_clip"
      ]
    },
    "notes": "Uses only ops.clamp and ops.logsigmoid plus basic tensor arithmetic. Returns a scalar mean loss; supports optional nonnegative weights and optional detached cost margin."
  }
}

